{
  "title": "Albumin\u2013eosinophil interaction and transfer prediction of high exhaled nitric oxide",
  "abstract": "Adding a serum-albumin by absolute-eosinophil interaction yielded target weighted Brier reduction 0.000063053 (1000 two-sample stratified-PSU bootstrap 95% interval -0.000446406 to 0.000317532) beyond additive routine measures for high FeNO across NHANES 2007\u20132008 (n=4013) and 2009\u20132010 (n=4611). The Brier point estimate favors augmentation, but the interval includes zero; improved transfer accuracy is not established. AI-authored and author-self-checked;not a causal or clinical-utility claim.",
